      "text": "To simplify the expression \\((x^5 + x^4 + x + 10) - (x^5 + 2x^4 - x^3 + 12)\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses.\n2. Combine like terms.\n\nLet's start by distributing the negative sign:\n\n\\[\n(x^5 + x^4 + x + 10) - (x^5 + 2x^4 - x^3 + 12) = x^5 + x^4 + x + 10 - x^5 - 2x^4 + x^3 - 12\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the like terms. The like terms are the terms with the same degree of \\(x\\):\n\n- The \\(x^5\\) terms: \\(x^5 - x^5 = 0\\)\n- The \\(x^4\\) terms: \\(x^4 - 2x^4 = -x^4\\)\n- The \\(x^3\\) term: \\(x^3\\) (since there is no other \\(x^3\\) term to combine with)\n- The constant terms: \\(10 - 12 = -2\\)\n\nPutting it all together, we get:\n\n\\[\n0 - x^4 + x^3 - 2 = -x^4 + x^3 - 2\n\\]\n\nSo, the simplified expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-x^4 + x^3 - 2}\n\\]",
